"cues": [
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 3.2,
"end": 9.121,
"text": "Emma asks: how many BAT-500 battery packs do we have in Manchester main stores?"
},
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 9.678,
"end": 11.454,
"text": "The model cannot open Ledgerline."
},
{
"block": "b1",
"t": 11.954,
"end": 16.11,
"text": "It can only write text, so it writes a request."
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 16.86,
"end": 25.138,
"text": "Here is the request, a tool call: the name check_stock, and one argument, item_code BAT-500."
},
{
"block": "b2",
"t": 25.695,
"end": 27.68,
"text": "Nothing has happened yet."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 28.43,
"end": 31.912,
"text": "First it meets tool.json, the tool's contract."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 32.412,
"end": 37.868,
"text": "The input schema asks for one field, item_code: a string, required."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 38.368,
"end": 39.935,
"text": "This request passes."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 40.562,
"end": 43.349,
"text": "But what if the model sent the number 500?"
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 43.883,
"end": 48.77,
"text": "The door refuses it: item_code should be string, got int."
},
{
"block": "b3",
"t": 49.27,
"end": 52.254,
"text": "Zero calls reach Ledgerline."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 53.004,
"end": 60.77,
"text": "Behind the door is tool.py: 26 lines of Python, running in Emma's own Ledgerline session."
},
{
"block": "b4",
"t": 61.27,
"end": 71.209,
"text": "It calls the legacy services: itm_get for the item, whs_list for the warehouses, then stk_query twice, for Manchester and for Leeds."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 71.959,
"end": 78.762,
"text": "Ledgerline answers in terse envelopes. rc: S. err_cd: null."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 79.262,
"end": 82.616,
"text": "An empty msg, and a data block of short codes."
},
{
"block": "b5",
"t": 83.116,
"end": 88.817,
"text": "Manchester: 5,400 on hand. Leeds: 1,200."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 89.567,
"end": 93.63,
"text": "The tool turns four envelopes into one clean, typed result."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 94.13,
"end": 100.318,
"text": "Each warehouse with its free stock, 6,600 in total, and 11 days of cover."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 100.875,
"end": 105.844,
"text": "842 bytes of legacy replies become 457."
},
{
"block": "b6",
"t": 106.344,
"end": 108.561,
"text": "Only this goes back to the model."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 109.311,
"end": 114.012,
"text": "And when the request is wrong? Ask for BAT-5000, which does not exist."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 114.512,
"end": 121.873,
"text": "itm_get answers rc E, ERR-ITM-0010, ITEM NOT FOUND."
},
{
"block": "b7",
"t": 122.5,
"end": 130.859,
"text": "The tool turns that into ok: false, the error in words, and a next step: use find_item with a description."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 131.609,
"end": 142.406,
"text": "So every tool has three parts: a contract the request must meet, code that talks to the old system, and one clean result or a clear error."
},
{
"block": "b8",
"t": 142.906,
"end": 147.306,
"text": "Open any tool in the toolbox, and you will find the same three."
}
]
}